public import Theory.SpecificGroups.AlternatingSix.ShadowLocal.HolomorphSubgroups.Automorphisms

/-!
# Subgroups of the cyclic-eight holomorph

This interface collects two intrinsic facts about C₈ ⋊ (Z/8)ˣ: its rank-one
subgroups with nontrivial Frattini subgroup are C₄, C₈, or Q₈, and the
automorphism groups of its normal subgroups have no primes other than two
and three. The first result does not require normality. All classification
alternatives are actual multiplicative equivalences.

Source: the local calculations in Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of
Quasithin Groups*, Lemmas 2.5.22 and 2.5.27, printed pp.567 and 569.
The identification with an actual Sylow subgroup of Aut(A₆) is separate.
-/
